    Draw and verify the norm parameter table openings in the first stage
    
    The first norm stage now draws the parameter table column positions from the
    chain after the table identity is fixed, opens them through the prover-side
    parameter table handle, and the verifier redraws the same positions, compares
    them with the message and verifies the openings against the plan's committed
    readers. A separate bias table draws its own positions; a packed table reuses
    the gain openings. The witness parameter vectors are length checked against the
    column domain. The fixture builds two small encoded tables from bounded row
    sources and commits them once; a positive chain and four negatives (changed
    position, changed symbol, missing bias openings, changed reader) pass through
    the real verifier.
    
    partial progress

